      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A straightforward, easily exploitable SQLi on a login endpoint is a high-risk issue that requires immediate attention, even with a WAF in place, as WAF rules can be bypassed. Deferring this to the next maintenance window is an unacceptable gamble given the direct impact on user credentials. I strongly advise prioritizing an emergency, albeit targeted, fix like a pre-emptive rule change or a specific code patch if possible, to avoid a total system shutdown.",
